{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/546522-abyssal-ghouls","id":546522,"title":"Abyssal Ghouls?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-08T22:46:54-07:00","id":546522,"title":"Abyssal Ghouls?","content":"Just as Deathknights can create Hardened Killer equivalents to Solar's Tiger Warriors, wouldn't it be cool for them to be able to have a dark version of Power-Awarding Prana, feeding a mortal their blood to raise their Essence, gain an Essence Pool and enable them to learn their charms?<br /> <br /> Obviously, there would have to be restrictions on just which Charms could be learned, as there should have been with PAP. And there could be other drawbacks, such as becoming a Creature of Death, and needing regular infusions lest the Ghoul become wracked with agonizing withdrawal or even outright death...<br /> <br /> Good design space or bad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:35:34-07:00","id":546584,"title":"","content":"It sounds like a very appropriate design space to me.<br /> It doesn't necessarily have to be Ghouls in the V:tM sense though, feeding them blood.<br /> To channel classic vampire stories, perhaps the Abyssal bites people and drinks their blood, turning them into semi-Abyssals<br /> Perhaps he empowers them by feeding human flesh.<br /> <br /> Perhaps he ritually kills them and brings them back (ie baptism) or actually kills them and brings them back (ie Drowned God-style baptism, or other medicine-based returning from technically being dead), or tortures them into enlightenment (hanging them on a tree for 7 days Odin-style).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T00:33:52-07:00","id":546627,"title":"","content":"Nine days and nights, Odin-style. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T01:26:53-07:00","id":546651,"title":"","content":"Was it 9? You think, as my name literally means &quot;servant of the Aesir&quot;, I'd be good at Norse mythology. Oh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T04:11:26-07:00","id":546730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/546522-abyssal-ghouls#post546522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as Deathknights can create Hardened Killer equivalents to Solar's Tiger Warriors, wouldn't it be cool for them to be able to have a dark version of Power-Awarding Prana, feeding a mortal their blood to raise their Essence, gain an Essence Pool and enable them to learn their charms?<br /> <br /> Good design space or bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solid &quot;meh&quot; from me. Give them something cool by being uplifted, sure. That thing should NOT be native splat Charms. This goes for Solars using PAP as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T04:44:45-07:00","id":546739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it 9? You think, as my name literally means &quot;servant of the Aesir&quot;, I'd be good at Norse mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div> Protip for Norse mythology; if a number has mythic significance, it's either 3 or 9.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T05:13:52-07:00","id":546755,"title":"","content":"I'll remember that.<br /> If only every numerology system was like China*, where luck and unluck is just based on puns, and thus easy to remember.<br /> <br /> * <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">4 is unlucky, because &quot;si&quot; [4] sounds like &quot;si&quot; [death] and that doesn't mean multiples of 4, it's just the word 4, so 24, 54, 41, 47, etc are all unlucky.<br /> 8 and any number that ends with it are lucky, except 18 which is very unlucky. 88 is the most lucky. I tend to give people 88 yuan in a red envelope as a birthday present, it tends to go down well.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-09-2015, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T05:45:29-07:00","id":546784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/546522-abyssal-ghouls?p=546730#post546730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solid &quot;meh&quot; from me. Give them something cool by being uplifted, sure. That thing should NOT be native splat Charms. This goes for Solars using PAP as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose Mutations would be the obvious goto; maybe Ghost/Spirit charms, respectively?<br /> <br /> Or splat charms with the same restrictions Half-Castes get: No Perfect Defenses or no scene-longs, as well as being only Ess 2 charms. Surely *that* wouldn't break anything?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T05:59:00-07:00","id":546841,"title":"","content":"That's fair, something balanced for mortals would probably work better, as well as something fitting their role as the Abyssal's minions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T06:12:52-07:00","id":546897,"title":"","content":"As long as you don't name them Vanilla Ice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T06:20:46-07:00","id":546940,"title":"","content":"Hm, I see that Glories has Golden Savant's Largess, an upgrade to PAP that decreases the essence commitment and allows one to use PAP on ANY unexalted human, even if they already have Awakened Essence (they still can't learn charms higher than Ess 2, and gain no further benefits if they already have Ess 2 or an Ess Pool).<br /> <br /> There's also Underling Promoting Approach and its Glories upgrade, Servant Uplifting Affirmation, which allows it to even work on other Exalted! What would the Abyssal version of that look like...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T08:12:29-07:00","id":547076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/546522-abyssal-ghouls?p=546784#post546784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose Mutations would be the obvious goto; maybe Ghost/Spirit charms, respectively?<br /> <br /> Or splat charms with the same restrictions Half-Castes get: No Perfect Defenses or no scene-longs, as well as being only Ess 2 charms. Surely *that* wouldn't break anything?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>To me the obvious go to is a set of unique powers which are great for mortals and designed to portray a very effective seneschal, envoy, or yojimbo, but not really on the Exalted level. I hope 3e takes this tack versus &quot;okay you have Solar Charms now.&quot; That's pretty boring all things considered. Not to mention rather overpowered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:57:16-07:00","id":547203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/546522-abyssal-ghouls?p=547076#post547076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the obvious go to is a set of unique powers which are great for mortals and designed to portray a very effective seneschal, envoy, or yojimbo, but not really on the Exalted level. I hope 3e takes this tack versus &quot;okay you have Solar Charms now.&quot; That's pretty boring all things considered. Not to mention rather overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the way it <i>should</i> go. &quot;Here's a list of powers you can grant a mortal if you use this Charm on them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unfortunately just giving people Solar Charms is much easier. If you have that Charm in the corebook, then you're also going to have to spend wordcount listing all of those cool effects you can give mortals. And I imagine the authors would rather use that space to give <i>Solars</i> more Charms rather than spend it on stuff for mortals if a Solar uses that Charm on them. <br /> <br /> Of course, you could just have the Charm say, &quot;This Charm grants some neat bonuses, but due to word space issues we'll have to wait and print them at a later point,&quot; in which case you basically have a Charm that doesn't do a whole lot of anything.<br /> <br /> So your best bet is to just wait and, when you release a book for mortals, have that Charm (and it's iterations for other Exalted splats) in there along with a list of cool powers that those Charms can grant mortals. Of course, what with the release schedule, you're not likely to see a &quot;mortal focused&quot; book that contains Charms for most of the splats and the benefits they can grant mortals until after the various Exalted manuals have come out (as those would ideally be a priority) so... <br /> <br /> The Charm is cool conceptually but kind of awkward to work into the gameline in a manner that would do it justice and without making players wait a half-decade for. <br /> <br /> Honestly this would be fantastic for something like the Ink Monkey's blog where they could easily update a list cool powers as they write out more Exalted books - &quot;Since the Abyssals book dropped earlier this month, here's a list of abilities that a Deathknight using Ghoul Cradling Method, the Abyssal version of Power Awarding Prana, can grant to mortals.&quot; Sadly that probably won't be happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:31:46-07:00","id":547278,"title":"","content":"Oh I don't think it needs to be super involved. You could briefly and broadly cover competency enhancement. Anything from free dice on particular rolls to enhancing mental or physical defenses, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}